### Description
This Terraform program sets up a Route 53 hosted zone for a domain name and creates an A record that maps a subdomain to an IPv4 address. The program includes the necessary resources and dependencies to ensure the correct setup.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "domain_name" {
  description = "The domain name to be managed in Route 53"
  default     = "example.com"
}

variable "subdomain_name" {
  description = "The subdomain name to map to an IPv4 address"
  default     = "www"
}

variable "ipv4_address" {
  description = "The IPv4 address to map the subdomain to"
  default     = "192.168.1.1"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "example_domain_zone" {
  name = var.domain_name
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "example_domain_record" {
  name    = "${var.subdomain_name}.${aws_route53_zone.example_domain_zone.name}"
  type    = "A"
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example_domain_zone.zone_id
  records = [var.ipv4_address]
  ttl     = 300
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
- **Variables**: Three variables are defined with default values:
  - `domain_name`: The domain name to be managed in Route 53 (default is `example.com`).
  - `subdomain_name`: The subdomain name to map to an IPv4 address (default is `www`).
  - `ipv4_address`: The IPv4 address to map the subdomain to (default is `192.168.1.1`).
- **aws_route53_zone Resource**: Creates a Route 53 hosted zone for the specified domain name.
- **aws_route53_record Resource**: Creates an A record that maps the specified subdomain to the given IPv4 address, referencing the zone ID from the `aws_route53_zone` resource. The TTL is set to 300 seconds.

