### Description of the Terraform Program

This Terraform program sets up a basic VPC with a public and private subnet. It then defines an EC2 Fleet using a launch template, which includes both On-Demand and Spot instances. The fleet will launch the newest AWS Linux 2 AMI available, with 5 On-Demand and 4 Spot instances.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "vpc_cidr_block" {
  description = "CIDR block for the VPC"
  default     = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

variable "public_subnet_cidr_block" {
  description = "CIDR block for the public subnet"
  default     = "10.0.1.0/24"
}

variable "private_subnet_cidr_block" {
  description = "CIDR block for the private subnet"
  default     = "10.0.2.0/24"
}

variable "instance_type" {
  description = "Instance type for the EC2 Fleet"
  default     = "t3.micro"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = var.vpc_cidr_block
  tags = {
    Name = "main-vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "public_subnet" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block        = var.public_subnet_cidr_block
  map_public_ip_on_launch = true
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"
  tags = {
    Name = "public-subnet"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "private_subnet" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block        = var.private_subnet_cidr_block
  availability_zone = "us-west-2b"
  tags = {
    Name = "private-subnet"
  }
}

resource "aws_launch_template" "ec2_fleet_launch_template" {
  name          = "ec2-fleet-launch-template"
  image_id      = "ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0"  # Placeholder for the newest AWS Linux 2 AMI
  instance_type = var.instance_type

  network_interfaces {
    associate_public_ip_address = true
  }
}

resource "aws_ec2_fleet" "ec2_fleet" {
  launch_template_config {
    launch_template_specification {
      launch_template_id = aws_launch_template.ec2_fleet_launch_template.id
    }
    override {
      subnet_id = aws_subnet.public_subnet.id
    }
    override {
      subnet_id = aws_subnet.private_subnet.id
    }
  }

  target_capacity_specification {
    default_target_capacity_type = "on-demand"
    on_demand_target_capacity    = 5
    spot_target_capacity         = 4
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "ec2-fleet"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Variables**: Default values are provided for the VPC CIDR block, public and private subnet CIDR blocks, and the instance type.
3. **VPC Resource**: A VPC is created with the specified CIDR block.
4. **Subnet Resources**: Two subnets are created within the VPC, one public and one private, each in different availability zones.
5. **Launch Template Resource**: A launch template is defined with the newest AWS Linux 2 AMI and the specified instance type. It also configures the network interface to associate a public IP address.
6. **EC2 Fleet Resource**: An EC2 Fleet is created using the launch template. It specifies 5 On-Demand and 4 Spot instances, with overrides for both public and private subnets.

