### Description
The Terraform program defined below will enable contributor insights on a DynamoDB table named "ExampleTableName". It includes the necessary resources and configurations to create the DynamoDB table and then enable contributor insights on it.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify a valid AWS region
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  name           = "ExampleTableName"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "id"

  attribute {
    name = "id"
    type = "S"
  }
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights" "example_contributor_insights" {
  table_name = aws_dynamodb_table.example_table.name
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider with a specific region (`us-west-2`).
2. Creates a DynamoDB table named "ExampleTableName" with a simple hash key (`id`) and uses the `PAY_PER_REQUEST` billing mode.
3. Enables contributor insights on the created DynamoDB table using the `aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights` resource, referencing the table name from the previously created DynamoDB table resource.

