### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster with the specified node type (`dax.r4.large`) and replication factor (`1`). It also sets up an IAM role required by the DAX cluster to operate. The program ensures that all necessary resources are created and properly referenced to meet the user's requirements.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify a valid AWS region
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_iam_role" {
  name = "dax_iam_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_dax_cluster" "my_dax_cluster" {
  cluster_name       = "my_dax_cluster"
  iam_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.dax_iam_role.arn
  node_type          = "dax.r4.large"
  replication_factor = 1
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider with a specified region.
2. Creates an IAM role named `dax_iam_role` with a trust policy allowing DAX to assume the role.
3. Creates a DAX cluster named `my_dax_cluster` using the previously created IAM role, with the specified node type and replication factor.

