### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) with an example CIDR block (`10.0.0.0/16`) and enables IPv6. The program includes a basic configuration for the VPC and sets up a security group ingress rule as an example of how to manage network access.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "example_vpc" {
  cidr_block               = "10.0.0.0/16"
  assign_generated_ipv6_cidr_block = true
  enable_dns_support       = true
  enable_dns_hostnames     = true
  tags = {
    Name = "ExampleVPC"
  }
}

resource "aws_security_group" "example_sg" {
  name        = "example_sg"
  description = "Example security group"
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.example_vpc.id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 22
    to_port     = 22
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "ExampleSecurityGroup"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **AWS VPC Resource**: A VPC is created with the CIDR block `10.0.0.0/16` and IPv6 enabled. DNS support and hostnames are also enabled.
- **Security Group**: A security group is created within the VPC to allow SSH access from any IP address (`0.0.0.0/0`). An egress rule is also added to allow all outbound traffic.

This configuration ensures that the VPC is set up with the necessary networking capabilities and security settings.

