This Terraform program creates an S3 bucket named `example_bucket` and configures the request payment for the bucket so that the bucket owner pays for all associated fees. The program also includes an accelerate configuration for the S3 bucket, although the specific status for acceleration is not specified in the prompt and defaults to `Enabled`.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Default AWS region
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "example_bucket" {
  bucket = "example-bucket-unique-name"  # Ensure the bucket name is globally unique
  acl    = "private"                     # Set the ACL to private
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_request_payment_configuration" "example_bucket_request_payment" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.id  # Reference the S3 bucket ID
  payer  = "BucketOwner"                   # Bucket owner pays for fees
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_accelerate_configuration" "main" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.id  # Reference the S3 bucket ID
  status = "Enabled"                       # Enable S3 bucket acceleration
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket named `example-bucket-unique-name` is created with private access control.
- **Request Payment Configuration**: The request payment configuration is set up to ensure the bucket owner pays for all associated fees.
- **Accelerate Configuration**: The S3 bucket's accelerate configuration is enabled to improve transfer speeds.

