### Description
The Terraform program defined below creates an S3 Glacier vault named `long_term_data_archiving_vault` for long-term data archiving. Additionally, it sets up a vault lock to ensure that the data stored in the vault cannot be deleted or modified without explicit permission.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify a valid AWS region
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault" "long_term_data_archiving_vault" {
  name = "long_term_data_archiving_vault"
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault_lock" "main" {
  vault_name = aws_glacier_vault.long_term_data_archiving_vault.name
  complete_lock = true
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Deny",
        Principal = "*",
        Action = "glacier:DeleteArchive",
        Resource = "${aws_glacier_vault.long_term_data_archiving_vault.arn}/*"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Deny",
        Principal = "*",
        Action = "glacier:InitiateVaultLock",
        Resource = "${aws_glacier_vault.long_term_data_archiving_vault.arn}"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider with a specific region (`us-west-2`).
2. Creates an S3 Glacier vault named `long_term_data_archiving_vault`.
3. Sets up a vault lock on the created vault to prevent deletion or modification of the data stored in the vault. The lock policy denies any actions that could delete or modify the vault or its contents.

