### Description
The Terraform program below sets up an AWS Backup Vault and an AWS Backup Plan for long-term data backup. The Backup Vault is named `long_term_data_backup_vault`, and the Backup Plan is named `long_term_data_backup_plan`. The Backup Plan includes a rule named `long_term_data_backup_rule` that targets the previously created Backup Vault.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_backup_vault" "long_term_data_backup_vault" {
  name = "long_term_data_backup_vault"

  # Optional attributes
  force_destroy = false
  tags = {
    Name = "LongTermDataBackupVault"
  }
}

resource "aws_backup_plan" "long_term_data_backup_plan" {
  name = "long_term_data_backup_plan"

  rule {
    rule_name         = "long_term_data_backup_rule"
    target_vault_name = aws_backup_vault.long_term_data_backup_vault.name

    # Optional attributes
    schedule          = "cron(0 12 * * ? *)"  # Daily backup at 12 PM UTC
    start_window      = 60                    # Start window in minutes
    completion_window = 120                   # Completion window in minutes
    enable_continuous_backup = false
  }

  # Optional attributes
  tags = {
    Name = "LongTermDataBackupPlan"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration creates an AWS Backup Vault and a Backup Plan with a daily backup schedule. The Backup Plan references the Backup Vault using a Terraform reference, ensuring proper dependency management.

