### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with a listener that uses a fixed-response action. The ALB will respond with a "Hello, World!" message whenever a request is made to it on port 80 using the HTTP protocol.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "my_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-load-balancer"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"

  subnet_mapping {
    subnet_id = "subnet-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with a valid subnet ID
  }

  security_groups = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]  # Replace with a valid security group ID
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "my_load_balancer_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.my_load_balancer.arn
  port              = 80
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "fixed-response"

    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "Hello, World!"
      status_code  = 200
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **Load Balancer (`aws_lb`)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with the name `my-load-balancer`. It is set to be internet-facing (`internal = false`) and uses the `application` type. The `subnet_mapping` block specifies the subnet where the load balancer will be deployed. Replace `"subnet-0123456789abcdef0"` with a valid subnet ID from your AWS account. The `security_groups` block specifies the security group associated with the load balancer. Replace `"sg-0123456789abcdef0"` with a valid security group ID.
- **Listener (`aws_lb_listener`)**: A listener is attached to the load balancer, listening on port 80 with the HTTP protocol. The `default_action` block specifies a fixed-response action, which returns a plain text message "Hello, World!" with a status code of 200.

