### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an "authenticate-cognito" action. The ALB will authenticate users against a Cognito User Pool. The program includes the necessary resources for the Cognito User Pool, User Pool Client, and User Pool Domain, and configures the ALB listener to use these resources for authentication.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "my_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-load-balancer"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]  # Replace with actual subnet IDs
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "my_load_balancer_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.my_load_balancer.arn
  port              = "443"
  protocol          = "HTTPS"

  default_action {
    type = "authenticate-cognito"

    authenticate_cognito {
      user_pool_arn       = aws_cognito_user_pool.my_cognito_user_pool.arn
      user_pool_client_id = aws_cognito_user_pool_client.my_cognito_user_pool_client.id
      user_pool_domain    = aws_cognito_user_pool_domain.my_cognito_user_pool_domain.domain
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_cognito_user_pool" "my_cognito_user_pool" {
  name = "my-cognito-user-pool"
}

resource "aws_cognito_user_pool_client" "my_cognito_user_pool_client" {
  name         = "my-cognito-user-pool-client"
  user_pool_id = aws_cognito_user_pool.my_cognito_user_pool.id
  generate_secret = true
}

resource "aws_cognito_user_pool_domain" "my_cognito_user_pool_domain" {
  domain       = "mycognitouserpooldomain"
  user_pool_id = aws_cognito_user_pool.my_cognito_user_pool.id
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Load Balancer (`aws_lb`)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with the specified subnets. Replace the subnet IDs with actual subnet IDs from your VPC.
3. **Load Balancer Listener (`aws_lb_listener`)**: A listener is added to the load balancer on port 443 using HTTPS. The listener uses the "authenticate-cognito" action to authenticate users against the Cognito User Pool.
4. **Cognito User Pool (`aws_cognito_user_pool`)**: A Cognito User Pool is created with the name "my-cognito-user-pool".
5. **Cognito User Pool Client (`aws_cognito_user_pool_client`)**: A Cognito User Pool Client is created for the user pool, with secret generation enabled.
6. **Cognito User Pool Domain (`aws_cognito_user_pool_domain`)**: A domain is set up for the Cognito User Pool with the name "mycognitouserpooldomain".

This configuration ensures that the load balancer authenticates users using Cognito, and all necessary resources are created and linked together.

