### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS EFS (Elastic File System) with specified tags. The program includes the necessary resources and configurations to ensure the EFS is properly set up and tagged.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "my_efs_file_system" {
  creation_token = "my-efs-file-system"
  performance_mode = "generalPurpose"
  throughput_mode  = "bursting"
  encrypted        = true

  tags = {
    Name        = "MyEFSFileSystem"
    Environment = "Production"
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system_policy" "main" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.my_efs_file_system.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action   = "elasticfilesystem:*"
        Resource = aws_efs_file_system.my_efs_file_system.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`).
2. **EFS File System**: An EFS file system is created with a creation token, performance mode, throughput mode, and encryption settings. Tags are added to the EFS file system for identification and categorization.
3. **EFS File System Policy**: A policy is attached to the EFS file system to allow all actions on the EFS resource. This policy uses the ARN of the EFS file system, which is obtained via a Terraform reference to the `aws_efs_file_system` resource.

