### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Elastic File System (EFS) with a specified system policy. The EFS is configured with default settings, and the policy allows all actions on the EFS from any AWS principal. The backup policy for the EFS is also set up with a default status.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "my_efs_file_system" {
  creation_token = "my-efs-file-system"
  encrypted      = true
  performance_mode = "generalPurpose"
  throughput_mode  = "bursting"
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system_policy" "my_efs_file_system_policy" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.my_efs_file_system.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action   = ["elasticfilesystem:*"]
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_efs_backup_policy" "main" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.my_efs_file_system.id
  backup_policy {
    status = "ENABLED"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up an EFS with encryption enabled, general-purpose performance mode, and bursting throughput mode. It also applies a permissive policy allowing all actions on the EFS from any AWS principal and enables the backup policy for the EFS.

